            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 47-year-old male patient, admitted on 30 December 2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection presenting as moderate-to-severe COVID-19 pneumonia. Diagnosis was established by PCR testing and supported by chest CT imaging demonstrating bilateral ground-glass opacities. Blood tests revealed elevated inflammatory markers including CRP and ferritin. Arterial blood gas analysis showed hypoxaemia requiring supplemental oxygen therapy. The patient was treated with dexamethasone, anticoagulation, and empirical antibiotics. Continuous pulse oximetry and regular vital signs monitoring were performed throughout the stay. Respiratory physiotherapy was initiated to support recovery. The patient showed gradual clinical improvement and was discharged on 11 January 2021 in a recovering condition. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks, monitoring oxygen saturation, respiratory function, and general recovery. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
